==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|bine}}, from {{inh|de|goh|bini}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*biniz}}, representing an ''-n-'' variant of Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*bijō}}. Cognate with {{cog|bar|Bein||bee}}, {{cog|osx|bini}}. Compare from ''*bijō'' the form ''Bei(e)'' in many dialects (Luxembourgish {{m|lb|Bei||bee}}, Alemannic {{m|gsw|Beie||bee}}).

